  "kind": "definition",
  "title": "Fourier-nonexceptional middle extension",
  "statement": "Let $j:U_0\\hookrightarrow\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}$ be a dense open immersion and\nlet $\\mathcal M$ be irreducible and lisse on $U_0$ (in the lisse\nconvention of [def-weil-pbc-constructible-complexes]). Its\nmiddle extension is\n*Fourier-nonexceptional* if, after geometric base change, it is\nneither a constant sheaf (up to a constant\nWeil twist) nor the restriction\nof an Artin–Schreier sheaf\n$\\mathcal L_{\\psi(ax)}$ for any $a$.",
  "source": {
